1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
SettleSight — AI Reconciliation Desk for PayPal Sellers

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Every month-end, small businesses spend painful hours matching PayPal transactions to invoices.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,400
SettleSight turns hours of spreadsheet chaos into minutes of automated clarity.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:18,500
Here is the reality: PayPal deducts processing fees, buyers send partial milestone payments...

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:24,500
...one transfer covers two invoices, and clients forget invoice reference numbers.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:30,250
Standard accounting spreadsheets break, forcing sellers to manually calculate fees and guess which payment belongs to which invoice.

7
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:37,500
Meet SettleSight. Powered by AG Studio 3.0 and PayPal Developer APIs,

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:46,000
in live mode it pulls PayPal Invoicing v2 and Transaction Search data; this demo uses a synthetic sandbox-shaped dataset.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,030
Our deterministic match engine runs on integer cents, instantly auto-reconciling clean payments with confidence 1.0.

10
00:00:54,030 --> 00:01:00,500
For complex transactions, the engine proposes scored candidates in the Exceptions Queue instead of guessing blindly.

11
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:08,000
Here, it identifies a fee-adjusted transaction: gross deposit minus standard PayPal processing fees equals net deposit.

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,250
Below it, partial milestone installments and combined multi-invoice payments are categorized with transparent confidence scores.

13
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:22,500
Need deeper insight? Our Reconciliation Auditor, built with AG Studio's Agent Framework, acts as your financial copilot.

14
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:30,500
When we ask to audit partial payments and fee discrepancies, the agent executes client-side tools with visible audit badges,

15
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:38,360
verifying that fees fall within tolerance of the open amount. The AI explains the exact reasoning in plain English before anything touches your ledger.

16
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:45,500
AG Studio gives merchants complete dashboard flexibility.

17
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:51,500
With one click, we enter layout mode to reposition widgets or expand our custom Aging Distribution chart,

18
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:57,140
highlighting overdue receivables across thirty, sixty, and ninety-day buckets. Every layout adjustment persists automatically to browser storage.

19
00:01:57,140 --> 00:02:03,500
Now, the seller takes action. When we click Approve in the Exceptions Queue,

20
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:10,000
our invariant math validator ensures the allocation is strictly valid—preventing over-allocations, currency mismatches, or rounding drift.

21
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,870
The Reconciliation Meter recalculates instantly, keeping the business owner firmly in control.

22
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:22,500
Finally, SettleSight drafts polite customer reminders and writes confirmed payments back to PayPal Invoicing v2 when connected to live credentials,

23
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:29,000
never mutating balances without seller approval. Zero manual spreadsheet formulas, zero guesswork, and deterministic mathematical accuracy.

24
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:36,560
Reconcile your PayPal ledger today in seconds. Thank you!
